      <marc:subfield code="a">Throughout history, rich and poor countries alike have been lending, borrowing, crashing and recovering their way through an extraordinary range of financial crises. Each time, the experts have chimed, &quot;this time is different&quot; claiming that the old rules of valuation no longer apply and that the new situation bears little similarity to past disasters. This audio book proves that premise wrong. Covering sixty-six countries across five continents, This Time Is Different presents a comprehensive look at the varieties of financial crises, and guides us through eight astonishing centuries of government defaults, banking panics, and inflationary spikes from medieval currency debasements to today&apos;s subprime catastrophe</marc:subfield>
